$\tfrac{1}{2}$ is the **only** unit fraction equal to a half; $\tfrac{1}{3}, \tfrac{1}{4}, \dots$ are all smaller.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},x=6cm,y=1cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(1.1,0);
\draw (0,0.12)--(0,-0.12);
\draw (0.5,0.12)--(0.5,-0.12);
\draw (1,0.12)--(1,-0.12);
\node[below] at (0,-0.12) {$0$};
\node[below] at (0.5,-0.12) {$\frac12$};
\node[below] at (1,-0.12) {$1$};
\draw[|<->|] (0.02,0.2)--(0.48,0.2);
\node[above] at (0.25,0.3) {less than a half};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

