The bars represent equal-sized wholes and show one half and one fifth.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black}]
\definecolor{fractionblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\fill[fractionblue!20] (0,1.5) rectangle (2.5,2.5);
\draw (0,1.5) rectangle (5,2.5);
\draw (2.5,1.5)--(2.5,2.5);
\node[left] at (0,2) {$\frac12$};
\fill[fractionblue!20] (0,0) rectangle (1,1);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,1);
\foreach \i in {1,...,4} {\draw (\i,0)--(\i,1);}
\node[left] at (0,0.5) {$\frac15$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which shaded part is larger?
